exd3 15. Qxd3 Bf5 16. Qd1 Qxa2 17. O-O Qxc4 {Gillam in his book featuring the
congress states that the game was prolonged to move 54, though he does not
give the continuation. BCM, Feb 1932, says that "the pieces were thinned down
to rook and knight against rook and bishop, and the weight of Black's
queenside pawns won in 55 moves."} 0-1

